G3606.def:
ὅθεν 
adv., 
whence; 
__(a) of direction or source: Matthieu 12:44, Luc 11:24, Actes 14:26 28:13; = ἐκεῖθεν ὅπου, Matthieu 25:24, 26 (cf. Thuc., i, 89, 3); ὅ. γινώσκομεν, 1 Jean 2:18; 
__(b) of cause, whence, wherefore: Matthieu 14:7, Actes 26:19, Hébreux 2:17 3:1 7:25 8:3 9:18 11:19.†

G3609.def:
οἰκεῖος, -α, -ον
(οἶκος), [in LXX for דּוֹד, שְׁאֵר, etc.; in Ésaïe 58:7, οἰ. τοῦ σπέρματος for בָּשָׂר ;] 
in or of the house (opposite to ξένος, ἀλλότριος); 
__(a) of things; τὰ οἰ., household affairs or goods; 
__(b) of persons, of the same family or kin; as subst., οἱ οἰ., kinsmen: 1 Timothée 5:8; with genitive of person(s), of the family of: metaphorically, τ. θεον, Éphésiens 2:19; τ. πίστεως (Lft., in l), Galates 6:10.†
SYN,: συγγενής, ἴδιος (see Cremer, 446; Deiss., BS, 123)

G3625.def:
οἰκουμένη, -ης, ἡ
(fern. Pres. pass. ptcp. of οἰκέω; sc. γῆ) [in LXX chiefly for תֵּבֵל, אֶרֶץ ;] 
the inhabited earth; 
__(a) in cl., the countries occupied by Greeks, as disting. from barbarian lands (Hdt., Dem., al.); 
__(b) in later writers, the Roman world: Luc 2:1, Actes 11:28 24:5; by meton., of its inhabitants : Actes 17:6 19:27; 
__(with) in LXX (Psaumes 23:1 71:8, al.) and NT, also of the whole inhabited world: Matthieu 24:14, Luc 4:5 21:26, Romains 10:18, Hébreux 1:6, Apocalypse 3:10 16:14; by meton. (ut supr.), Actes 17:31, Apocalypse 12:9; 
__(d) of the Messianic age, ἡ οἰ. ἡ μέλλουσα = ὁ αἰὼ ὁ μέλλων: Hébreux 2:5.†

G3650.def:
ὅλος, -η, -ον, 
[in LXX chiefly for כֹּל ;] 
of persons and things, whole, entire, complete; 
__1. of indefinite ideas, with subst. anarth.: Luc 5:5, Actes 11:26 28:30, Tite 1:11; ὅλον ἄνθρωπον (an entire man; see Field, Notes, 93), Jean 7:23; ὅλη Ἰερουσαλήμ (= πᾶσα Ἰ, Matthieu 2:3; see Bl., §47, 9), Actes 21:31. 
__2. Definite, with art.; 
__(a) preceding subst.: Matthieu 4:23, 24 Luc 8:39, 1 Corinthiens 12:17, al.; 
__(b) following subst.: Marc 1:33, Luc 9:25, Jean 4:53, Actes 21:30, al.; 
__(with) between art. and subst., where subst. is an abstract noun (Plat., al.). 
__3. Attached to adj. or verb: Matthieu 13:33, Luc 13:21, Jean 9:34, al.; adverbially, δι ̓ ὅλου (MM, xviii), Jean 19:23.

G3659.def:
ὄμμα, -τος, τό in cl. chiefly poët.; 
[in LXX for עַיִן (עַיִן (Proverbes 5:1-23, Wis.2:1-24, 4Ma.3:1-21)* ;] 
an eye: p1., Matthieu 20:34 Marc 8:23.†

G3667.def:
ὁμοίωμα, -τος, τό
(ὁμοιόω), [in LXX for דְּמוּת, תַּבְנִית, תְּמוּנָה, etc. ;] 
that which is made like something; 
__(a) concrete, an image, like­ness (Psaumes 106:20, Eze.1:5, 1Ma.3:48, al.) : Apocalypse 9:7; 
__(b) abstract, like­ness, resemblance: Romains 5:14 6:5 8:3, Philippiens 2:7; ἐν ὁ. εἰκόνος, Romains 1:23.†
SYN.: εἰκών (which see), ὁμοίωσις

G3674.def:
ὁμοῦ
adv. (ὁμός), 
together; 
__(a) prop., of place: Jean 21:2, Actes 2:1; 
__(b) without idea of place: Jean 4:36 20:4.†

G3694.def:
ὀπίσω 
adv. 
of place and time, 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחַר and cogn. forms ;] 
__1. prop., as in cl., adv., 
__(a) of time (not in NT); 
__(b) of place, back, behind, after: Matthieu 24:18, Luc 7:38; τὰ ὀ., Philippiens 3:13; εἰς τὰ ὀ., Marc 13:16, Luc 9:62 17:31, Jean 6:66 18:6 20:14. 
__2. By a usage not found in cl., and in LXX representing the Heb. prep. אַחַר (Bl., § 40, 8; Thackeray, Gr., 46 f.), but also prob. general in vernacular (M, Pr., 99), as prep. with genitive; 
__(a) of time, after: Matthieu 3:11, Marc 1:7 Jean 1:15, 27 1:30; 
__(b) of place, behind, after: Matthieu 4:19 10:38 16:23-24, Marc 1:17, 20 8:33-34, Luc 9:33 14:27 19:14 21:8, 2Pe 2;10, Ju 7, Apocalypse 1:10 12:15; in constr. praegn. (see Swete on Re, l.with), Jean 12:19, Actes 5:17 20:30, 1 Timothée 5:15, Apocalypse 13:3.†
